  "scope": "Only the new lambda=0 prime-baseline reduction in Decision15 equations5-8 and its consumer wording; completed E16 remains unchanged.",
  "clause_assessments": [
    {
      "clause": "xi_reflection_and_coordinates",
      "status": "accepted",
      "finding": "H0=xi(s)/8 with reflected s=1/2-iz/2 sends strip heights0,4,8 to Re s=1/2,5/2,9/2. Constants cancel with total boundary mass1."
    },
    {
      "clause": "elementary_Gamma_harmonic_growth",
      "status": "accepted",
      "finding": "s has its zero at z=-i outside; pi factor has affine harmonic logarithm; Gamma(s/2) is zero-free on Re(s/2)>=1/4 within the finite strip. At most linear-plus-logarithmic horizontal log-modulus growth is paid by exponential Poisson kernels. Note25 lower-boundary integrability plus these factors pays the critical-line zeta log, including multiple real zeros."
    },
    {
      "clause": "zeta_pole_correction",
      "status": "accepted",
      "finding": "s-1 vanishes at z=i and contributes +G(X,1). Its cancellation of the zeta pole is retained explicitly; log zeta is not silently treated as harmonic across s=1."
    },
    {
      "clause": "K_Fourier_factor_and_safe_line_coefficient",
      "status": "accepted",
      "finding": "u=exp(2ax) yields Khat=(1/2)sech(4omega); at omega=(log n)/2 it is1/(n^2+n^-2). Safe-boundary minus interior coefficient is exactly n^-9/2/(n^2+n^-2)-n^-5/2=-n^-5/2/(1+n^-4). Evenness preserves the stated cosine and no extra factor2."
    },
    {
      "clause": "Euler_log_and_interchanges",
      "status": "accepted",
      "finding": "At Re s=5/2 and9/2, prime-power Euler-log series converge absolutely and uniformly in the imaginary coordinate; Lambda_vM(n)/log n is1/k for n=p^k and zero otherwise, hence <=1. Absolute weighted summability justifies all interchanges and gives J0=L-P+G(X,1)."
    },
    {
      "clause": "uniform_prime_tail",
      "status": "accepted_after_integer_domain_explicit",
      "finding": "For integer N>=2, |P-PN|<=sum_(n>N)n^-5/2<=integral_N^infinity u^-5/2 du=(2/3)N^-3/2, uniformly in all real X. For a real cutoff use its integer part. The lead explicit-domain insertion was the sole bounded clarification."
    },
    {
      "clause": "inequality_direction_and_missing_margin",
      "status": "accepted_with_scope",
      "finding": "J0>=0 implies only L>=P-G. Exclusion of a declared d,r defect requires the unproved strict upper inequality L<P-G+sin(a)d/cosh(ar), with both boundary and prime tails below that margin. No favorable critical-line signed mean estimate or exclusion follows."
    }
